<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2012/Flash-2.jpg" alt="Initial layout for the conformation portrait of a horse" width="600" height="466" /></p>
<p>I painted over the outline of the horse with a fine liner brush. &nbsp;I used thin paint with Liquin and left it to dry for a couple of days then I applied a thin wash of burnt sienna and ivory black over the top of it. This is a backwards way of painting.</p>
<p>After wiping down the wash with a paper towel the outline has faded &nbsp;considerably in some areas, but is still faintly visible. &nbsp;I now have a good foundation for starting the painting proper and I haven't lost the toning by making corrections to the outline. Yet.</p>